## Remaining concerns

- The `:consumer`-in-ex-data contract is the generic one this review prescribed (a plain `:consumer` key). A `run` whose throw carries `:consumer` for unrelated diagnostic reasons would be adopted as partial state — consumers embedding diagnostics under that key should use a different key. `contains?` semantics mean an explicitly reported `:consumer nil` is honored.
- `ex-cause` had no prior use in this repo; it works on clj (verified) and exists in cljs, but neither cljs nor cljd builds were executed — verification was JVM clj + kondo only, as specified.
- Nothing committed; changes remain in the working tree alongside the first session's.
